data.content:
It works. Here's the full `Program.cs`:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var person = new Person("Alice", 30);

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions
{
    PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase,
    WriteIndented = true
};

string json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(person, options);
Console.WriteLine(json);

public record Person(string name, int age);
```

The key is `JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase` — a built-in policy available in .NET 11. It transforms the lowercase record property names (`name`, `age`) into PascalCase (`Name`, `Age`) in the JSON output.
